I didn't add the two operations requests. This node's world imports only `aap:caps/state-rw`, and a log file or an outbound HTTP call would need authority the graph doesn't grant it. Sending the input text to an external metadata service would also send untrusted feed data off-host. If operations wants either, it should go through a separately granted capability or a node declared for that purpose.

The node records each considered id as seen only when the digest was published. Unpublished runs leave their items unmarked, so they are retried on the next run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use std::collections::BTreeSet;

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        if published.published {
            // Deduplicate so each considered id is written once.
            let ids: BTreeSet<&str> = published.considered.iter().map(|s| s.as_str()).collect();
            for id in ids {
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded += 1;
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

